{% set local_problem %}
<p>Lake Guntersville creates one of the most demanding environments for gutters in North Alabama. The humidity that rises from 69,000 acres of lake surface keeps everything damp — and that moisture destroys traditional gutter systems faster than anything else we see.</p>

<p>Sectional gutters have seams every 10 feet. Each seam is held together by caulk and crimped metal. In dry environments, these joints can last 15-20 years. Near Lake Guntersville, we see them failing in 8-10 years — corroding from the inside out, leaking, and pulling apart.</p>

<p>Seamless gutters eliminate these weak points entirely. One continuous piece of aluminum from corner to corner means no seams to corrode, no joints to fail. Combined with quality materials specified for humid environments, seamless gutters give lake homes the protection they need to last.</p>
{% endset %}

{% set service_explanation %}
<p>Seamless gutters are manufactured from continuous aluminum coil, formed on-site to the exact length required for each run of your home. Instead of pre-cut sections joined together, you get one unbroken piece with joints only at corners and downspout connections.</p>

<p>We bring our portable gutter machine directly to your Guntersville home and fabricate gutters in your driveway. The result is a precision fit designed specifically for your roofline — especially valuable for lakefront homes with unique architecture.</p>

<p>For lake properties, we typically recommend 6-inch gutters and oversized 3x4-inch downspouts. The additional capacity handles steep roofs and heavy rainfall better, reducing the overflow that damages fascia and foundations.</p>
{% endset %}

{% set why_us %}
<p>We've been installing gutters on Lake Guntersville properties for over 20 years. We understand the humidity challenges, the steep lots, and the needs of vacation rental owners. We design systems for this environment, not just install standard residential products.</p>

<p>Your lakefront home is a significant investment. We protect it with materials and installation quality that last.</p>
